.env.*
# Packaged templates are source, not secrets. Without this negation the .env.*
# rule above silently keeps templates/*/*/.env.example out of the repo, and the
# stacks that ship one fail to scaffold from a clean checkout. Real .env files
# stay ignored everywhere, including inside generated projects.
!initra/templates/**/.env.example
test-*/
